  },
  {
   "index": 28,
   "tag": "p×4",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 1315,
   "text": "Scores like Net Promoter Score (NPS), CSAT, and Customer Effort Score already sit inside most reporting cadences, which makes them cheap to borrow. Tie your work to their movement, and segment wherever the data allows.\nMeridian could say that NPS among trial users on the redesigned onboarding was 51 against 34 for the legacy flow, which lands far harder than any blended average. Verbatim feedback ",
   "counts": {
