  {
   "index": 34,
   "tag": "ul",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 1444,
   "text": "“Measuring the User Experience” by Tom Tullis and Bill Albert is the definitive guide to UX metrics. It covers everything from task-based measurements to survey design to statistical analysis, and it’s written for practitioners, not academics.\nJared Spool’s “The $300 Million Button” case study is a classic example of how a single UX change (removing a mandatory registration step) generated massive",
